title: Genesis 9 – Blessings, Commandments and Promises
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 9: God blesses Noah and his sons, gives meat and the death penalty, sets the bow in the cloud, and Noah curses Canaan.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-9-blessings-and-covenant.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 9 study
# (posts 6615, 6617, 6618).

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 9 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 9: Blessings, Commandments and Promises
sub: Meat and Blood • The Bow in the Cloud • The Curse of Canaan
refs: Genesis 9:1-29
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Blessings and commandments
--- Be Fruitful, and Multiply
kicker: vv. 1–3
sub: Every Moving Thing That Liveth Shall Be Meat
scripture: Genesis 9:1-3 | mark: Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth; Every moving thing that liveth shall be meat for you
p: God blesses Noah and his sons, gives commandments and a covenant with all living things in the earth. Blessings, commandments and promises: this is the pattern of things with God when those who are faithful and saved by His grace walk with God. God tells Noah and his sons to be fruitful and multiply, birthing all nations of man. To that end, He reminds them that all animals are meat to eat, with no restrictions.

--- But Flesh with the Blood
kicker: v. 4
sub: The Life Thereof Shall Ye Not Eat
scripture: Genesis 9:4 | mark: flesh with the life thereof, which is the blood thereof, shall ye not eat
p: Of the clean and unclean animals they may eat, but only the clean for sacrifice to God, being they represent Christ Jesus. There is no restriction on what they can eat, provided they drain the blood, the life thereof. Of that they should not eat.

--- Clean and Unclean
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 9:3–4
fig: Genesis 7:2 | Genesis 7:2 | As we saw in chapter 7, Noah had seven pair, male and female, of every clean beast, that he could give sacrifice in thanksgiving to God for saving his family in chapter 8. [[Genesis 8:20]]
fig: Hebrews 9:10 | Hebrews 9:10 | This was replaced for a time for Israel with strict dietary laws against eating unclean beasts under Mosaic law, which, along with the priestly and carnal ordinances, were done away with in Christ. [[Colossians 2:16-17]]

--- Blood for Blood
kicker: vv. 5–6
sub: For in the Image of God Made He Man
scripture: Genesis 9:5-6 | mark: Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of God made he man
p: God institutes the death penalty, capital punishment for the shedding of blood. Before the flood, from Cain on, the requirement for blood didn’t exist, and evil propagated. Here, God established a new understanding for man: that we were to enforce His law, blood for blood, *for in the image of God made he man*. [[Genesis 4:15]]

--- Bring Forth Abundantly
kicker: v. 7
sub: Replenish the Earth
scripture: Genesis 9:7
p: God commands again that man be fruitful and multiply. Replenish the earth, bringing forth life abundantly.

=== The bow in the cloud
--- My Covenant with You
kicker: vv. 8–11
sub: Neither Shall There Any More Be a Flood
scripture: Genesis 9:8-11 | mark: neither shall there any more be a flood to destroy the earth
p: God promises all life that He would never destroy the earth and all living things again by flood.

--- The Token of the Covenant
kicker: vv. 12–17
sub: I Do Set My Bow in the Cloud
scripture: Genesis 9:12-17 | mark: I will look upon it, that I may remember the everlasting covenant between God and every living creature of all flesh that is upon the earth
p: He gives the rainbow as His reminder, a token of the covenant between Him and the earth.

=== The sons of Noah
--- Shem, Ham, and Japheth
kicker: vv. 18–19
sub: Of Them Was the Whole Earth Overspread
scripture: Genesis 9:18-19 | mark: Ham is the father of Canaan
p: And so the Bible tells us of Shem, and Ham, and Japheth, and that Ham is the father of Canaan. Of these three was the whole earth overspread. The next chapter of Genesis goes into detail of the generations and nations of them, but for the next part of chapter 9, we need to know Ham’s son Canaan. [[lesson:genesis-10-table-of-nations|Genesis 10]]

--- Noah Began to Be an Husbandman
kicker: vv. 20–23
sub: He Drank of the Wine, and Was Drunken
scripture: Genesis 9:20-23
p: Noah, retired from ark building, becomes a husbandman, a grower of grapes. The Bible says he drank his own wine and became drunk, and that Ham saw his nakedness as he was passed out in his tent, and that he called his brothers to see.

--- What His Younger Son Had Done
kicker: vv. 24–25
sub: Cursed Be Canaan
scripture: Genesis 9:24-25 | mark: knew what his younger son had done unto him
p: There is a lot of speculation as to what this means. Most agree that Ham did something unspeakable to Noah in his condition. The Bible doesn’t say that, and generally, God’s word isn’t shy about naming the acts done by the wicked. The implication comes from Noah’s reaction and punishment, which is severe.

--- Blessed Be the {Lord} God of Shem
kicker: vv. 26–27
sub: Shem Blessed, Japheth Enlarged, Canaan a Servant
scripture: Genesis 9:26-27
p: He curses Canaan to be servants of Shem and of Japheth, the nations that spring from each son. He blesses Shem with the blessing of the {Lord} God, as the oldest. This is the blessing of Christ through his seed. And he blesses Japheth with abundance, to be enlarged greatly. There is a lot of speculative theology based off this curse, and some of the conclusions drawn aren’t supported in scripture. Take secular takes on a spiritual matter with the appropriate grains of salt. [[Luke 3:36]]

--- Nine Hundred and Fifty Years
kicker: vv. 28–29
sub: The Last of the Long-Lived Men
scripture: Genesis 9:28-29
p: Noah lives 350 years following the flood, a total of 950, but he is the last of the antediluvian long-lived men.

=== The spiritual application
--- The Deeper Things of God
kicker: Application
sub: Mercy, Judgment, Grace and Salvation
p: There are, of course, deeper things of God: His promises and blessings, the salvation of Christ mirroring the salvation of the ark. But the predominantly secular focus on hidden meaning, esoteric knowledge, the hyperfocus on race and genealogies of man, conspiracies and Jewish fables have all but flooded out those truths in the minds of man. Even saved Christians get sucked in to endless strivings about the meaning of some of what’s revealed to us in God’s word. [[Titus 1:14]]
callout: What’s important to Bible believing Christians is to draw spiritual application from scripture, to understand the things of God which He revealed to us from the beginning. Mercy, judgment, grace and salvation. The fallen nature of man and the prevalence of sin while we are in the flesh. The righteousness of the living God.

--- Give Thanks
center: As we give thanks to God for our salvation and the blessings He bestows, the same way Noah gave thanks after leaving the ark, we should try to keep in mind the spiritual, looking forward to that better country and the feast of Christ Jesus, knowing that man’s relationship with God has always been, from the beginning. Amen. [[Hebrews 11:16]]
